      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230523/assets/93d069bfebd0d91cac459285a0e92cd14b5eab90bc465d7728b80b4f6fcbd47a.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Given that $y=f(x)$ is periodic with period $5,$ what is the value of $f(-37)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the period is $5,$ if we add (or subtract) any multiple of $5$ from the input, the output stays the same.\n\nSo, we can keep adding $5$ to the input until we get to an input that we see in the graph:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-37) & =f(-37+5) \\\\  & =f(-37+2\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =⋯ \\\\  & =f(-37+8\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =f(3) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
